{"availability":"available","full":"eyereasoner/eyeling","name":"eyeling","description":"A Notation3 (N3) reasoner in JavaScript.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":19,"forks":6,"created":"2025-11-20T22:40:48Z","updated":"2026-09-23T18:23:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyeling/","topics":[],"demo":"https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyeling/playground","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:11.113Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:11.113Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:11.113Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:44:11.113Z","stars":19,"forks":6}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A compact Notation3 (N3) reasoner in JavaScript.","Eyeling aims to make knowledge itself computationally accountable, so every conclusion can be derived, checked, and explained. It does this by keeping reasoning close to explicit facts, rules, and proofs rather than hidden assumptions or opaque workflows. As a compact Notation3 reasoner for JavaScript, Eyeling is designed to fit into practical systems while remaining inspectable enough for researchers, engineers, and agents to understand why a result follows. The ambition is not just to process data, but to support a culture of verifiable knowledge: conclusions that can be exchanged,…","Eyeling is designed for people who want a small, inspectable reasoner that can run N3 rules in Node.js, the browser, tests, and RDF-oriented data pipelines."],"features":["Notation3 reasoning in a small JavaScript package — facts, quoted formulas, and N3 rules are parsed and reasoned over directly.","Forward and backward chaining — => rules derive new facts, while <= rules act as goal-directed definitions.","Backward proving inside forward rules — forward-rule bodies are solved with the backward engine, so rules can use derived predicates and built-ins without materializing everything first.","Built-ins in rule bodies — N3 programs can combine logical rules with computations such as math, string, datatype, list, time, and web-oriented predicates.","Streaming RDF Messages — supports RDF Messages streams, enabling Eyeling to fit into streaming RDF pipelines."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eyereasoner/eyeling/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d08d97026b54bc7c3e8a0c2933a23d478d9596a4e15c5b1c02da61d891519102","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:11.227Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:11.227Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A compact Notation3 (N3) reasoner in JavaScript.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eyereasoner/eyeling/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Eyeling is designed for people who want a small, inspectable reasoner that can run N3 rules in Node.js, the browser, tests, and RDF-oriented data pipelines.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eyereasoner/eyeling/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d08d97026b54bc7c3e8a0c2933a23d478d9596a4e15c5b1c02da61d891519102","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eyereasoner/eyeling/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:11.228Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-23T18:23:35Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eyereasoner/eyeling/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:11.231Z","hash":"d08d97026b54bc7c3e8a0c2933a23d478d9596a4e15c5b1c02da61d891519102","originalBytes":47534,"storedBytes":47534,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["rdf","eyeling","examples","lib","input","const","output","facts","rules","run","store","test","npm","when","rdf-js","log","derived","proof","browser","built-in","message","reasonstream","rule","api","prefix","bash","true","backward","cli","rdfjs","terms","persistent","compatibility","custom","example","package","require","tests","console.log","fact","forward","mode","quads","reason","reasoning","result","source","triple","add","javascript","closure","false","stream","syntax","await","before","built-ins.","my-